The seat-balanced retest of the founding claim (U6) completed:
starter 16, v1 10, random 14 over 40 episodes. Read together
with T6, the lineage's first-evening narrative inverts: the
"always take lethal" change was celebrated on a confounded
receipt, and the tracker now holds the correction at the same
prominence as the claim. This is the MOAT/TLUF discipline
doing its work — a False-adjacent finding kept visible, the
registry more accurate than the story.

Standing after Round 4:
  - Champion title: SUSPENDED in fact (the charter keeps v1
    listed until evidence names a successor; the registry no
    longer asserts v1 exceeds the starter).
  - v3b and v3c remain co-candidates (U3, U4): both beat v1 in
    both seat legs. Their anchor tests against the STARTER —
    the honest baseline — are running: v3b xreq_726f3ec8 +
    xreq_fedb848e; v3c xreq_1cd68615 + xreq_9a3fe5ae.
  - The veteran seat remains the strongest single bloc per
    appearance across every test tonight (roughly a third of
    all episodes). The gap to the field is the real target;
    heuristic micro-tuning around the starter is not.ROUND 5 — Anchor tests against the starter (EE 369-370)

The co-candidates were re-anchored on the honest baseline, the
pristine starter, seat-balanced, 40 episodes each:

  v3b vs starter (xreq_726f3ec8 + xreq_fedb848e, $0.108):
    starter 17, v3b 9, random 14. REFUTED as an advance (F3).
  v3c vs starter (xreq_1cd68615 + xreq_9a3fe5ae, $0.141):
    v3c 16, starter 12, random 12. OPEN (U7) — nominally
    ahead, legs split by seat.

Standing at EE 370, stated plainly: after ~300 hosted episodes
and five variants, no variant has a verified claim to beating
the bundled starter bot. v3c is the only live candidate. The
veteran field (random seat) took roughly a third of every
test's episodes throughout — the gap to the field is in deck
construction and multi-way threat judgement, not in the swing
scoring this bracket has been tuning. Next honest moves, in
order: (1) a higher-n confirmation of v3c vs starter;
(2) a deck-construction universe (the precon mix is untouched
in every variant so far); (3) a scout study of the veterans'
decks from played-card traces, which the Round 2 data already
holds in part (U5).

Streaming: at Will's direction (EE 370) this phext is streamed
to wbic16/human as we play — each MVO pass lands there as a
commit, so the public record and this tracker are one text.ROUND 6 — Ascend: three universes at once (EE 370)

Will's direction: iterate and ascend; unlock collaboration
through unexpected teamwork. Three tests launched in parallel:

1. CONFIRMATION of U7 at honest scale: v3c vs starter, 100
   episodes seat-balanced (xreq_4de08476 + xreq_9634c73f).
   The claim graduates or dies at this n.

2. DECK UNIVERSE (v4): every variant so far played the Archer
   precon. v4 = the Warrior precon bot, byte-identical stock
   heuristics (sha256 d14e338a...), vs the Archer starter —
   the deck axis tested alone (U8). Two further precons wait
   on the shelf: Mage, and an Archer/Warrior splash.

3. TEAMWORK UNIVERSE (v5): in a free-for-all where the last
   hero standing scores, our paired seats have played as
   strangers. v5 = v3c heuristics + a team protocol:
   - Family by geometry: paired seats sit two apart in our
     rosters ((0,2), (1,3)); each seat computes its partner
     from its own seat index. No channel, no communication —
     the seating IS the protocol.
   - While any outsider lives: never swing at or target the
     partner (hero or minion, attack or card effect); helpful
     effects MAY land on the partner's minions; both seats
     focus fire on the highest-life outsider (+3 swing, +2
     card targeting).
   - When no outsider remains, the family fights as usual.
   Metric is the family's: an episode counts for the pair if
   either seat wins (U9). Control: a v1 pair, independent.
   Recorded caveat: the partner arithmetic assumes our paired
   test rosters; a lone league seat would run the focus rule
   only. Policy: emise-cac-v5-team:v1 (diff vs v3c: the
   teamcalc block + three gated call sites, 51 diff lines).ROUND 7 — Three verdicts; a champion crowned on evidence (EE 371)

CONFIRMATION (U7 -> T7, TRUE): v3c vs starter at 100 episodes:
v3c 42, starter 29, random 29 (legs 23-9 and 19-20). With the
anchor test, cumulative 58-41 over 99 decisive episodes, two
independent seat-balanced tests in the same direction. The
face-pressure tilt is the lineage's first verified advance.
v3c is champion — the title now rests on receipts, not story.

DECK AXIS (U8, OPEN leaning True): Warrior stock beat the
Archer starter in both legs, 14-7 combined (random 19 — the
veteran feasted on two stock bots, its highest share yet).
The precon is a real lever, roughly the size of the v3c tilt.

TEAMWORK (U9 -> T8, TRUE as stated): the coordinated v5 pair
took 27 of 40 episodes; the independent v1 pair took 6; the
veteran, focus-fired by both twins, fell to 7 (17.5%, against
a ~30% baseline all night). Collaboration is the largest
effect measured in this tracker — larger than seat 0's edge
per pair, larger than any heuristic. Its isolated size (over
and above the v3c edge) is U10, test defined.

Standings at EE 371: champion v3c (solo). Next universes, in
leverage order: (1) v6 = champion heuristics ported to the
Warrior deck; (2) U10 isolation (team v3c vs independent v3c);
(3) U8 confirmation at n=100. League submission remains
Will's call alone; the solo candidate would be v3c or v6.UNIVERSE v3a — mid-tier elimination everywhere (EE 368-369)

Design: one change from champion v1 — a swing that eliminates
ANY hero scores 25 (playerLife(o) check), above ordinary hero
swings (4 + 2*power) and most trades, below premium minion
kills. Hypothesis (from Round 2): v2's per-target lethal was
right in direction, wrong in price (flat 100 falsified, F1).
Policy: emise-cac-v3a:v1, version 746afc4e.

Test (xreq_b431294f + xreq_40b57886, 40 episodes, $0.119):
  leg a (v3a seats 0,2): v3a 17, v1 3, random 0
  leg b (v3a seats 1,3): v3a 2, v1 12, random 6
  combined: v3a 19, v1 15, random 6

Verdict: INCONCLUSIVE — registry U2 stays OPEN. The legs
disagree because seat 0 (T6) dominates at this sample size;
combined exposure is seat-balanced, so 19-15 is an unbiased
but noisy estimate (34 decisive episodes, well inside chance).
The round's real yield is T6 itself: the arena's geometry
outweighs the heuristics we have been tuning. Any future A/B
in this tracker must either rotate seat 0 at fine grain or
run enough episodes for the seat effect to average out.UNIVERSE v3b — neighbor first, others measured (EE 368-369)

Design: v1 unchanged for the next living player (lethal = 100);
an elimination of any OTHER hero scores 25. Rationale: Round 2
showed the neighbor focus is real geometry (F1's mechanism,
U1), while v3a asked whether a mid-tier price alone suffices.
Policy: emise-cac-v3b:v1, version a76bc1e4.

Test (xreq_d96f76a2 + xreq_cfc84e67, 40 episodes, $0.199):
  leg a (v3b seats 0,2): v3b 10, v1 5, random 5
  leg b (v3b seats 1,3): v3b 8, v1 7, random 5
  combined: v3b 18, v1 12, random 10

Verdict: LEADING CANDIDATE — registry U3 stays OPEN. Unlike
v3a, v3b won both seat assignments, so its edge is not a seat
artifact; but 18 of 30 decisive episodes is inside chance, and
the charter (T5) moves the championship only on evidence.
Path to True: a confirmation run at 100+ episodes.UNIVERSE v3c — face pressure (EE 368-369)

Design: hero swings score 10 + 2*power (was 4 + 2*power),
near minion-kill value; the lethal rule is v1's, unchanged.
Tests the veteran face-race pattern (T4) as a tilt rather than
a copy: F2 already refuted face-racing as a law, but a moderate
tilt was untested. Policy: emise-cac-v3c:v1, version c4129321.

Test (xreq_4fcb50e2 + xreq_97938efd, 40 episodes, $0.180):
  leg a (v3c seats 0,2): v3c 11, v1 5, random 4
  leg b (v3c seats 1,3): v3c 7, v1 6, random 7
  combined: v3c 18, v1 11, random 11

Verdict: CO-CANDIDATE — registry U4 stays OPEN, same standing
as U3: both legs won, margin inside chance. v3b and v3c test
different mechanisms and both lean positive; a playoff between
them, or a combined variant (neighbor discipline + face tilt),
is the next universe to open — after the T1 retest settles what
the champion itself is worth (U6).